<PolicyLayout title="Terms of service" description="Terms for using Filo's Android learning app, website, class features, optional backups and AI-assisted study tools.">
  <p>These terms describe the use of the Filo Android learning app and public website, provided by the Filo project team. Read them alongside our <a href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Using Filo</h2>
  <p>Filo supports learning activities for students and instructors. Use it only when authorized to participate in the relevant class and follow your school's rules. Provide accurate account information, choose your correct role and protect access to your Google account and device.</p>
  <h2>Responsible use</h2>
  <p>Do not impersonate another person, access classes or records without permission, disrupt the service, bypass assessment controls, upload harmful files or use Filo to harass others. Share only content you are entitled to use and follow your instructor's assessment and academic integrity rules.</p>
  <h2>Your materials and class records</h2>
  <p>You retain your rights in materials you provide. By uploading, submitting or sharing them, you allow Filo and its service providers to store, process and display them as needed for the features you choose. Class content is available according to class permissions. Your school and instructors remain responsible for their teaching, grading and recordkeeping decisions.</p>
  <h2>AI study tools</h2>
  <p>AI-generated answers, flashcards and practice questions can contain errors or omissions. Check them against your learning materials and your instructor's guidance. Do not treat AI output as an official grade or authoritative answer. Only send source material you are allowed to share with the AI provider, and avoid private or sensitive information.</p>
  <h2>Offline work, submissions and backups</h2>
  <p>Some saved materials work offline. Sign-in, synchronization, AI generation, official assessments and submissions require a connection where indicated by the app. A queued action or an interrupted request is not confirmation that work was received; check the final status and retry or contact your instructor when needed.</p>
  <p>Optional Drive backup depends on your Google permission, connection, available storage and Google's service. Keep independent copies of important work. Removing local files does not remove Drive backups, and turning backup off pauses uploads.</p>
  <h2>Preview availability and changes</h2>
  <p>Filo is currently provided as a preview. Features may change, become unavailable or contain defects. Continuous availability, error-free operation and recovery of every lost file cannot be guaranteed. Tell your instructor promptly if a technical problem affects an assessment or submission.</p>
  <h2>Stopping use and deleting your account</h2>
  <p>You may stop using Filo and use its account deletion option. Instructors must delete their owned classes first. Submissions and grades remain in instructors' records as Deleted User after account deletion; existing Google Drive copies remain in your Drive. See the Privacy policy for details.</p>
  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>Google, Supabase, GitHub and the website hosting provider have their own applicable terms. These terms do not replace your school's policies or the terms of services you use through Filo.</p>
  <h2>Questions and updates</h2>
  <p>For help, use the Filo team contact details provided with your app or by your school. Project information is available in the <a href="https://github.com/rogiie234/filo-app">Filo project repository</a>. Do not publish private student or account information in public issues.</p>
  <p>Changes to these terms will be posted here with an updated date. Nothing in these terms is intended to remove rights that applicable law gives you.</p>
</PolicyLayout>
